### Topic 47 - Spring Security Fundamentals
### Use with the VS Code "REST Client" extension: click "Send Request" above each block.
### Start the app first:  mvn spring-boot:run

@host = http://localhost:8080

### 1. Public URL - no login needed -> 200
GET {{host}}/api/public/notice

### 2. Protected URL without credentials -> 401 Unauthorized
GET {{host}}/api/me

### 3. Protected URL with HTTP Basic (REST Client encodes user:password for you) -> 200
GET {{host}}/api/me
Authorization: Basic student student123

### 4. Wrong password -> 401
GET {{host}}/api/me
Authorization: Basic student wrongpass

### 5. Admin URL as a normal USER -> 403 Forbidden
GET {{host}}/api/admin/stats
Authorization: Basic student student123

### 6. Admin URL as ADMIN -> 200
GET {{host}}/api/admin/stats
Authorization: Basic admin admin123

### 7. POST works without a CSRF token because CSRF is ignored for /api/** -> 201
POST {{host}}/api/feedback
Authorization: Basic student student123
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "message": "Loved the security lesson!"
}

### 8. CORS preflight from an allowed origin -> 200 with Access-Control-Allow-Origin
OPTIONS {{host}}/api/me
Origin: http://localhost:3000
Access-Control-Request-Method: GET
Access-Control-Request-Headers: Authorization

### 9. CORS preflight from an unknown origin -> 403 "Invalid CORS request"
OPTIONS {{host}}/api/me
Origin: http://evil.example.com
Access-Control-Request-Method: GET
